{"type":"lesson.started","request_id":"85b49d30-0432-4012-9192-76ceca5ce8cf","title":"Chance a dart lands in a circle inside a square"}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"85b49d30-0432-4012-9192-76ceca5ce8cf","step":{"id":"s1","script":"Assume the dart lands somewhere in the square, with equal areas equally likely. What is the chance it lands inside this inscribed circle?","ops":[{"op":"text","id":"title","region":"C1","content":"A random dart"},{"op":"figure","id":"target","region":"left","frame":{"x":[-1.4,1.4],"y":[-1.4,1.4],"axes":"none"},"marks":[{"kind":"polyline","id":"square","points":[[-1,-1],[1,-1],[1,1],[-1,1]],"closed":true},{"kind":"circle","id":"circle","center":[0,0],"r":1}]},{"op":"text","id":"assumption","anchor":{"el":"title","side":"below","gap":0.06},"content":"Equal areas → equal chances"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"85b49d30-0432-4012-9192-76ceca5ce8cf","step":{"id":"s2","script":"Call the circle's radius r. The square's side spans two radii, so its side length is two r.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"dimensions","on":"target","marks":[{"kind":"point","id":"center","at":[0,0]},{"kind":"segment","from":{"at":"center"},"to":[1,0],"label":"r"},{"kind":"measure","from":[-1,-1],"to":[1,-1],"label":"2r"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"square_area","anchor":{"el":"assumption","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"A_{\\text{square}}=(2r)^2=4r^2"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"85b49d30-0432-4012-9192-76ceca5ce8cf","step":{"id":"s3","script":"The shaded circle is the successful region. Its area is pi r squared; compare that with the whole square's area.","ops":[{"op":"figure","id":"success","on":"target","marks":[{"kind":"shade","inside":"circle"}]},{"op":"equation","id":"circle_area","anchor":{"el":"square_area","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"A_{\\text{circle}}=\\pi r^2"}],"checkpoint":{"question":"What area ratio gives the chance of landing inside the circle?","expected_gist":"Circle area divided by square area."}}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"85b49d30-0432-4012-9192-76ceca5ce8cf","step":{"id":"s4","script":"Divide the circle's area by the square's area. The radius cancels, giving pi over four: about a seventy-eight point five percent chance.","ops":[{"op":"equation","id":"probability","anchor":{"el":"circle_area","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"P=\\frac{\\pi r^2}{4r^2}=\\frac{\\pi}{4}\\approx78.5\\%"},{"op":"figure","id":"result","on":"target","marks":[{"kind":"text","at":[0,0.48],"text":"78.5%","size":"large"}]}],"checkpoint":null}}
